<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TIGER WHEELS LIFTS HALF YR SHR 39 PERCENT.</title>
<headline>TIGER WHEELS LIFTS HALF YR SHR 39 PERCENT.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended December 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)  28.8	   vs   20.7</p>
<p>    Attrib income	13.17	  vs    8.47</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		17.49	  vs   11.02</p>
<p>    Tax		     4.55	  vs    2.76</p>
<p>    Interest paid	 0.78 (gain) vs    1.95 (paid)</p>
<p>    Turnover	    208.26	  vs  166.13</p>
<p>Full name: Tiger Wheels Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it was cautiously optimistic that</p>
<p>its performance levels could be maintained for the remainder of</p>
<p>the current financial year, provided no unforeseen circumstances</p>
<p>arose. The group pays dividends at year-end.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
